course: dictionary
lesson: 3116
title: Who is an elector?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An elector is a person who has the right to vote in an election. The word is about power to choose. In the sentence «In 2016, it was reported, Hillary Clinton got about three million more votes nationwide than Donald Trump but lost, because he won more electors», the clue is "because he won more electors". So electors decide who wins, not just how many people voted.
explain: In the USA, electors are the members of the Electoral College, and they formally choose the President. The sentence «The US president is chosen by the Electoral College: each state has a number of electors» shows that each state has its own number. Read the words around elector to find out which meaning is being used.
explain: Some words hold more than one meaning. In history, «An Elector was one of the princes who chose the Holy Roman Emperor.» That is a different use of the same word. When you meet a word that could mean more than one thing, check the sentence and ask: what does it mean here?
fact: An elector is a person who has the right to vote in an election.
fact: The electorate means all the voters together.
fact: In the USA, the Electoral College is made of electors who formally choose the President.
fact: To win the US presidency, a candidate needs 270 of the 538 electors.
fact: In history, an Elector was a prince who chose the Holy Roman Emperor.
exercise: «Whoever reaches 270 of the 538 electors becomes president.» In this sentence, what is an elector? | *A member of the Electoral College who helps choose the president | A shop that sells sweets | A road sign on a motorway
exercise: «The electorate» means what? | A town hall with a big clock | A quick chat about politics | *All the voters together
exercise: «News reports said Joe Biden won the 2020 election with 306 electors to Donald Trump's 232.» How many electors did Joe Biden win? | 270 | 538 | *306 | 232
test: «The US president is chosen by the Electoral College: each state has a number of electors, most states give all of theirs to the winner there, and 270 of the 538 electors are needed to win.» How many electors are needed to win? | 232 electors | Just 10 electors | All 538 electors | *270 of the 538 electors
test: «In almost every state the winner takes all of them.» What does winner takes all mean? | Electors are given away to the losers | *The candidate who wins a state gets all of that state's electors | Each voter gets one elector | Every state splits its electors equally
exam: «In history, an Elector was one of the princes who chose the Holy Roman Emperor.» In history, what was an Elector? | A teacher in a school | A soldier who guarded a castle | A king who ruled alone | *A prince who chose the Holy Roman Emperor
